<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Congo Reform Association</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1904–1913</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Congo Reform Association was a humanitarian campaign founded in 1904 by the journalist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/e-d-morel">E. D. Morel</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roger-casement">Roger Casement</a> to expose abuses in King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leopold-ii">Leopold II</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congo-free-state">Congo Free State</a>. Using mass meetings, photographs and press campaigns in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, it helped force <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a> to annex the Congo in 1908 and was dissolved in 1913.</p></div>
